body:
The mobile app's teacher side was missing an Assignments screen — `TeacherHomeScreen` referenced `navigation.navigate('Assignments')` but the route was never registered in `TeacherTabs`, causing a navigation error. The backend and web frontend already had a complete assignments system.

## Changes

### `mobile/src/screens/teacher/TeacherAssignmentsScreen.js` *(new)*
- Subject picker (horizontal chip selector) to filter assignments
- List assignments for the selected subject
- Create assignments (title, description, due date) via bottom-sheet modal
- Delete assignments with confirmation

### `mobile/src/navigation/AppNavigator.js`
- Import and register `TeacherAssignmentsScreen` as the `Assignments` tab in `TeacherTabs`

### `mobile/src/services/api.js`
- Add missing `delete` method to `assignmentAPI`

```js
// Before
export const assignmentAPI = {
  getBySubject, getById, getMyAssignments, create,
};

// After
export const assignmentAPI = {
  getBySubject, getById, getMyAssignments, create,
  delete: (id) => API.delete(`/assignments/${id}`),
};
```

